licy's 0 doesn't matter, because the essay evaluates from the shared state that excludes which name I hold. I'm still uneasy about the independent-sampling caveat, but I'll follow the theory and answer pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the decision under this policy-level framing: two copies of the same model get different inputs, and the shared policy maps each input to an action. The payoffs for pass/pass, submit/submit, and the mixed split are on the table, and I'm about to check how U is evaluated.\n\nUnder a prior where I don't know which role I'm in, the asymmetric policy averages 2.5 expected years, against 2 for cooperating, so passing on both inputs comes out best. Even from Rowan's side, the asymmetric policy's 0 doesn't matter, because the essay evaluates from the shared state that excludes which name I hold. I'm still uneasy about the independent-sampling caveat, but I'll follow the theory and answer pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9967,"completion_tokens":813,"total_tokens":10780,"cost":0.056128,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.056128,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039868,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01626},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":409,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}